# No immutable rule for /assets/*. With not_found_handling "single-page-application" a missing
# /assets/<old-hash>.js is answered with index.html (200), and `_headers` matches the request URL,
# so a rule on /assets/* would also mark that fallback HTML immutable. Hashed assets keep the
# Workers default (public, max-age=0, must-revalidate + ETag): a cheap 304 on repeat visits.

# Security headers that need no per-environment value. The Content-Security-Policy is not set here: this file
# cannot give /lesson-frame.html and /sso-bridge their own policy (rules merge, and one cannot replace a header
# set by an earlier rule). See docs/adr/0022-security-headers-and-csp.md, "Workers static assets".
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(self), payment=(), usb=()
